hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27328","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Yazid, meaning Ibn Habib, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Talha ibn Yazid ibn Rukana, that his maternal aunt, the sister of Masud ibn al-Ajma, narrated to him that her father said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the Makhzumi woman who stole a velvet garment: We will ransom her with forty ounces. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For her to be purified is better for her. So he ordered her and her hand was cut, and she is from Banu Abd al-Ashhal, or from Banu Abd al-Asad."
